# Coverage / claims (CCMS) UX

Coverage/Claims owns: payers, plans, eligibility, coverage, authorization/preauth, claims, claim documents, enhancements, denials, settlement vs payer, reconciliation, payer workflows, coverage analytics.

**SoT:** CCMS (`microservices/ccms-service`). Canonical UI: `src/components/ccms/` + `/dashboard/ccms/*`.

Also follow `.cursor/rules/ip-billing-ward-cross-module.mdc`.

## Must not duplicate Billing

CCMS does not own cash/card/UPI capture, receipts, or the OpdBill ledger. Billing and Coverage integrate through **explicit contracts** (allocation, payer responsibility, settlement recording). Do not post silent bill mutations from a claims screen without the existing billing APIs.

## Complementary UIs (do not merge without approval)

| Surface | Job |
|---|---|
| `components/ccms` + `/dashboard/ccms` | **Ops desk** — cases, preauth queue, claims, settlement, master payers |
| `counsellors-desk/coverage` | **Session intake** — discuss coverage/estimate during counselling |
| IP `CoverageContextBlock` | Rail **display** of coverage context |
| `/dashboard/insurance`, `/dashboard/finance/insurance` | Retired redirects to CCMS — do not rebuild standalone insurance |

Do not clone Underwriting / VisitPolicies / Estimate panels across CCMS and counselling. Extend the owner for that job. Prefer `lib/hooks/useCoverageForm.ts` over a second hook.

## UX / safety

Eligibility and auth states are controlled workflow states. Documents and PHI respect permissions. Failed TPA/integration must not look approved. Settlement/reconciliation states stay explicit. Analytics/reports must not mutate cases.

Counsellor session styling stays scoped to `.counselling-session` — do not globalize it onto CCMS ops pages.
